      "message": "Hello everyone.\n\n1- If aw_dev_set_afe_module_en() fails (e.g., DSP message timeout), we print the error but still proceed to print the \u0027cur state\u0027 and return 0. Should we return ret instead of 0 to let the upper layers handle the failure?\n\n2- Global State: I see g_algo_rx_en is being evaluated. If this device features a stereo setup (dual AW88261 instances), could a global variable cause a race condition between the left and right amps? Might be safer if tied to the struct aw882xx context.\n\nThat\u0027s all thank you",
